     * Normalizes a URI path by ensuring it has exactly one leading slash.
     * <p>
     * The original implementation removed all but one leading slash but failed to
     * add a slash when the input did not start with one. This could cause a
     * malformed path to be interpreted as a host or other URI component,
     * leading to potential URL spoofing or resolution errors. The updated
     * method trims excess leading slashes, guarantees a single leading slash,
     * and handles empty or null inputs safely.
